    "q-166756": {
      "dom_id": "question-166756",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The road between Mary's home and the community park is straight. What is the distance between Mary's home and the point halfway between Mary's home and the community park?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The distance between Mary's home and the halfway point is$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$meters.",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190309/assets/d06fbf44c15301b9fc764823eb6d51652d9fe9426b5aa01b764e4b409d9dc6d5.png)\n\n \n\nLet $H$ be Mary's home (located at $x=0\\,\\text{m}$) and let $P$ be the community park (located at $x=960\\,\\text{m}.$)\n\nTo find the number ${x}_{m}$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$ between Mary's home and the community park, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+960}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{960}{2} \\\\  & =480.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190309/assets/8bba4fb81dc0a1e303a1f2bbe5e9d02fe159dfac83f29153401a2e7fda0b8df0.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the point that lies halfway between Mary's home and the community park is $480\\,\\text{m}$ from Mary's house.",
