  \n                                        \n                                        They met at a distance of$\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$meters from their home.",
      "worked_solution": "Mary and Sam meet when they are at the same distance from home. At this moment, their graphs intersect.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190309/assets/8afd4e9a8374ebe1e35200f6172e7fac9ef6c132d84e532c3ac44c25cb838a0d.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(11,300).$ So, Mary and her brother met $11$ minutes since they started moving at a distance of $300\\,\\text{m}$ away from their home.",
